      "reasoning": "Verified. Line 344 comment '// ✅ Provide default implementations when possible' sits above `expect class Analytics` (lines 345-348) whose members `track`/`flush` have no bodies — so the example itself provides no default implementation, and expect declarations cannot carry implementation bodies at all. The skill's own DON'T section (lines 353-360, `expect class Platform { fun calculateSomething(): Int { ... } }` with '// Complex logic here won't compile') confirms bodies are illegal in expect declarations. The DO guidance is therefore internally contradictory and misleading about what expect can do. Legitimate minor documentation defect as characterized."
    }
